    "body": "## Summary\n\n- `vertico-count` is already 13 in `sp-completion`, but the mini-frame was only `vertico-count + 2` frame lines tall. `sp-minibuffer` enlarges the minibuffer text by two steps of `text-scale-mode-step` (about 1.17), so its lines are taller than the frame's and the last candidates were cut off when scrolling.\n- `sp-mini-frame--lines` now multiplies the line count by that scale and rounds up.\n- Doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Not run in Emacs (none in the container); the cause is read from the code.\n- If the bottom is still cut, the scale in `sp-mini-frame--lines` is the thing to adjust.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01MfEFZ7KDkwwcifErLfjf4X)_",
